WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.360
Hello, I'm Gav.

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:02.193
I'm Dan.

00:00:02.193 --> 00:00:03.370
We're the Slow Mo Guys.

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:04.610
Not in the back garden today.

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:06.590
Yeah, we're here with Blue Man Group.

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:07.423
Alright, lads.

00:00:07.423 --> 00:00:08.680
I always associate Blue Man Group

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:12.230
with, you know, amazing
visuals, creativity

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:14.210
and generally just making a huge mess.

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:15.510
But today we're bowling.

00:00:18.295 --> 00:00:19.128
Flip.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:26.060
So when you have a 16 pound
bowling ball suspended

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.640
from the ceiling, it's very
important to have, well,

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:29.680
something to catch it with.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.340
Well, luckily Slow Mo Guys and Blue Man

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:32.280
have got quite a lot in common,

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.630
'cause our first target is
gonna be multicolored jelly.

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:37.017
This could take a while to
whisk up in this giant buck--

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:40.135
Nevermind.

00:00:40.135 --> 00:00:41.650
Whoa!

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:43.350
Get in there, there we go.

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:48.750
Dan, do the honors.

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:52.260
Absolutely. Ah.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.600
Look at that, that's absolutely spot on.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:55.433
Good job guys.

00:00:55.433 --> 00:00:56.330
We should smash this before it melts.

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:57.180
Yes, we should.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.133
Hey, this bit's mine.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:04.750
Aww.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:05.890
Got a good feeling about this one.

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:07.430
Yeah, You ready?
Count it off.

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:10.613
Okay. 3, 2, 1, drop.

00:01:14.665 --> 00:01:15.498
No.

00:01:15.498 --> 00:01:16.376
It just bounced like a trampoline.

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:17.209
No way.

00:01:43.209 --> 00:01:46.980
If we sort of combined a bowling
ball with a cheese grater

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.136
somehow, it would separate
it into lovely segments.

00:01:50.136 --> 00:01:52.270
Ahh, that would be even more
practical for these guys.

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:53.490
That'll be our next collaboration.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:54.750
Yeah, next feeding time.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:55.583
Yeah.

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:02.830
Usually, I have to do this on my own

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:05.105
y'know I usually have to
deal with crappy jobs.

00:02:05.105 --> 00:02:06.620
Gavin says he's sorting the cameras out

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:09.523
but he's probably just
sitting there playing games.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:12.010
Everything just gets trashed

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:15.289
I spend hours doing this,
it's soon just annoying.

00:02:15.289 --> 00:02:17.830
Y'know, you're a really good listener.

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:19.200
It's just kinda strange

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.385
'cuz you don't really have ears.

00:02:21.385 --> 00:02:23.080
This is definitely the most important part

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.220
of the Slow Mo Guys, erm

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:26.937
just the prep and setup and stuff

00:02:26.937 --> 00:02:29.120
not the cameras or any of the editing

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:32.620
and that's why uh- why she left me

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:34.940
but, um- look at me now.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:37.320
I'm doing this important work

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:38.470
fill out these sweet balls

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:40.380
but this is what Biance
does on her weekends

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:41.270
with uh- Jay Z.

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:42.863
Another power couple, yeah.

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.260
I've always wondered, uh- y'know

00:02:48.154 --> 00:02:48.987
are you blue all over?

00:02:48.987 --> 00:02:52.870
Or is it just like, uh,
just-just wondered, y'know.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:54.723
Just... Curious.

00:03:02.685 --> 00:03:05.102
What-what... Guess I blew it.

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:10.280
Nice stack, there, bet that took a while.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:11.113
It-it did, yeah.

00:03:11.113 --> 00:03:12.030
Oh, it did? Alright.

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:12.863
You ready to smash it now?

00:03:12.863 --> 00:03:13.696
Ready.

00:03:13.696 --> 00:03:14.700
K, cool. Alright.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.343
3, 2, 1, Drop!

00:03:19.556 --> 00:03:22.680
Ooh, bloody nora!

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:25.823
Tell you what, I'm not cleaning that up.

00:03:25.823 --> 00:03:26.697
Well, I mean-

00:03:26.697 --> 00:03:29.030
I am not cleaning that up.

00:04:21.388 --> 00:04:23.971
Whaddya know, that is useful.

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:26.057
That is incredibly useful.

00:04:26.057 --> 00:04:28.060
It's like a chest arse.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:28.893
It is.

00:04:28.893 --> 00:04:29.726
A charse.

00:04:29.726 --> 00:04:30.830
Yeah, or chanus.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.560
We should definitely buy him a cork

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:34.170
for his next birthday.

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:35.854
That is out of hand.

00:04:35.854 --> 00:04:37.289
it's dribbly.

00:04:37.289 --> 00:04:38.130
Here you go.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:39.130
What do you want from me?

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:39.980
Put it on.

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:43.101
I clearly can't do it, look
how steady my hands are.

00:04:43.101 --> 00:04:45.523
Brilliant, I'm done with
this responsibility.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:48.604
They were counting on you, Daniel.

00:04:48.604 --> 00:04:49.960
You can- you can do this just uh-

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:50.930
This is a lot of responsibility

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:52.603
this is precarious, okay- yeah.

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:57.403
I don't want to waste his chest juice.

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:00.043
It's straight from the heart.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:05.082
Nobody move.

00:05:05.082 --> 00:05:06.183
Slowly back away.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:09.653
You ready?

00:05:09.653 --> 00:05:11.130
I am looking forward to it- I'm ready.

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:11.963
You good?

00:05:11.963 --> 00:05:12.920
Ready as heck.

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:16.533
Good, alright- 3, 2, 1, drop.

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:24.783
That made a mess. That
is a hell of a mess.

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:30.150
Gotta say, I love the 3D effect

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:32.580
that we've ended up here
for this masterpiece.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:34.263
Yeah, I mean uh- we
sat out to make a mess.

00:06:34.263 --> 00:06:35.980
I think that's a great success to us.

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:37.000
Probably deadly, too

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.100
so like, if you touch-

00:06:41.390 --> 00:06:42.700
Good work.

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:43.830
Love it.

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:44.710
We get to keep this?

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:45.543
Thanks, guys.

00:06:45.543 --> 00:06:46.450
That's excellent.

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:48.980
Aw, brilliant, guys.

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:50.150
Thank you so much.

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:52.443
Y'know, I think I'm gonna
put this in my bathroom.

00:06:54.203 --> 00:06:55.260
Look at that.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:57.490
Might just buy a mat for underneath it.

00:06:57.490 --> 00:06:58.323
Whaddya think?

00:07:02.785 --> 00:07:04.740
Well that was a lovely
amount of destruction

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:06.540
but it would be almost criminal

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:07.770
if we made a bowling video without

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:09.100
getting a strike somehow.

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:10.100
I'm not good at bowling though

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:11.270
so I can't really do that.

00:07:11.270 --> 00:07:12.820
You are rubbish, I've seen you bowl.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:14.070
I suggest that we build one of those

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:16.173
like, learner ramp cheat things.

00:07:18.490 --> 00:07:21.460
I think that the blue men
took it to the extreme

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:23.390
and they made this monstrosity

00:07:23.390 --> 00:07:26.460
so, uh, looks like
something from one of those

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:30.117
bridge constructing games,
yeah- it looks like Meccano

00:07:30.117 --> 00:07:31.635
but for grownups.

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:37.070
So we're not just here to
make a video with the blue men

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:39.219
we also want to find out
what they're made of.

00:07:39.219 --> 00:07:40.052
Yeah, do a little bit of research.

00:07:40.052 --> 00:07:40.910
For instance, did you know there was

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:42.900
only ever 3 blue men at any one time?

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:44.953
Yeah, and when a blue man dies

00:07:44.953 --> 00:07:48.400
they don't decompose, the
head just rolls clean off

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.210
and then a new blue man
is born from an egg.

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:51.450
Yeah, I found these 3 heads, y'know

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:52.880
covered from the other corner.

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:53.713
I think these ones are from

00:07:53.713 --> 00:07:55.200
the '90s in the Vegas Show, actually.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:58.020
Yeah, so let's ball a boy
into the sight of the end

00:07:58.020 --> 00:07:59.530
and see what these ones are made of.

00:07:59.530 --> 00:08:00.863
Alright, placing bets on
what's inside this one

00:08:00.863 --> 00:08:01.773
whaddya think?

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:04.300
It could be anything, I don't know.

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:05.870
I reckon grape juice.

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:06.703
Grape juice?

00:08:06.703 --> 00:08:08.300
Yeah, okay- are you ready, then?

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:09.133
Ready.

00:08:09.133 --> 00:08:12.013
Alright, 3, 2, 1, drop.

00:08:15.226 --> 00:08:16.650
What is that?

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:17.653
It's a cereal.

00:08:19.455 --> 00:08:20.288
Lucky charms?

00:08:41.291 --> 00:08:44.230
I feel bad for the blue men
having to witness that one.

00:08:44.230 --> 00:08:47.490
I know, bits of skull
fragment went everywhere.

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:48.984
Should we make them do it again?

00:08:48.984 --> 00:08:52.170
Alright, 3, 2, 1...

00:08:56.444 --> 00:08:59.630
That's gruesome! God!

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:02.363
Oh, that looks like...
That looks delicious!

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:28.820
All right, final head.

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:30.240
This one's more of like a recreation

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:32.200
